# Keep LF in files Linux executes or parses, whoever commits them.
#
# Preventive, not a fix for an observed break: the repository is committed from
# Windows, and a shell script or systemd unit that arrives with CRLF does not
# run at all -- `#!/bin/sh\r` is not an interpreter, and the error says
# "Permission denied" or "bad interpreter", neither of which mentions line
# endings. Cheap to state here, expensive to diagnose on a server.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
*.timer         text eol=lf
deploy/**       text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
